  "script": "The 2022 Ford Mustang Shelby GT500 Heritage Edition boasts impressive power and style, pushing the limits of performance cars. Its prominent front grille details a fierce Cobra emblem, symbolizing its high-performance pedigree. The carbon fiber rear wing enhances aerodynamics, reflecting a design focused on performance. A distinctive rear wing boosts downforce, a hallmark of the GT500's racing-inspired design. Under the hood, a supercharged 5.2-liter V8 ripples with 760 horsepower and 625 lb-ft of torque. Inside, the steering wheel features the Cobra emblem, a nod to its performance roots. Lightweight Recaro seats with Shelby branding define the interior's sporty character. A black front grille with the iconic snake logo emphasizes the aggressive design of the GT500. Originally priced around $80K, its value reflects its limited edition status and performance edge. With 760 hp, it overpowers the Camaro ZL1's 650 hp. Both charge down the quarter-mile at around 11 seconds flat. So, would you choose the GT500's raw power and heritage, or do you lean towards another legend?",
